{
  "title": "cee-exporter",
  "uid": "cee-exporter",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "editable": true,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Events received / sec",
      "description": "Delivery rate, not file activity. This counts event batches arriving from CEE; it does not count distinct filesystem operations, and nothing here deduplicates.\n\nCEE redelivers an event it cannot retire, at the heartbeat interval, forever. Measured on this estate: one event from 2026-08-14 20:35:21, byte-identical on every delivery — same path, same timeStamp, same inode — six deliveries in 65 seconds alongside seven heartbeats. That is not throughput, and the consumer cannot tell the difference: an empty HTTP 200 is the whole acknowledgement CEE expects for an event batch (its binaries carry no CheckEventResponse literal at all), so a replay is indistinguishable from real traffic at the wire.\n\nRead it with Events per heartbeat: a value pinned at 1.00 means every delivery is arriving on the heartbeat clock, which is the replay shape.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "cee-prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(cee_events_received_total[5m]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "eps",
          "decimals": 3,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Writes / sec → evtx",
      "description": "Records per second reaching the configured output — the .evtx file on this deployment. cee_events_written_total counts what the writer accepted, so this is the rate the audit file actually grows at.\n\nIt should track Events received exactly; a persistent gap is backlog and Queue depth says how much. Deliveries, not distinct filesystem operations: nothing here deduplicates, and CEE on this estate redelivers one event from 2026-08-14 on every heartbeat. See Events per heartbeat. A replayed event is written again on every delivery, so this is also the rate duplicate records accumulate.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "cee-prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(cee_events_written_total[5m]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "wps",
          "decimals": 3,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Events in range",
      "description": "Absolute count of events received over the dashboard's selected time range — the number behind the rate. Over a 65-second window against this estate it reads 6, matching the six CheckEventRequest batches counted on the wire in that span.\n\nFollows the time picker, so widening the range widens the count. Deliveries, not distinct filesystem operations: nothing here deduplicates, and CEE on this estate redelivers one event from 2026-08-14 on every heartbeat. See Events per heartbeat.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "cee-prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(cee_events_received_total[$__range]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
