    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Deliveries per heartbeat",
      "description": "Event deliveries divided by heartbeats across all publishers — a replay detector derived from counters that already existed.\n\nRead the STEADINESS, not the level. The level is arbitrary: heartbeats are summed over every publisher while events arrive from CEE alone, so this estate sits at 0.20 (0.1 events/s against 0.5 heartbeats/s from six publishers), not at 1.00. What matters is that it does not move.\n\nA value that holds exactly constant means deliveries are clocked by the connection rather than produced by filesystem activity — CEE redelivering an event it cannot retire. Real traffic is bursty and this value moves. Zero means nothing is being delivered at all.\n\nA signature, not a proof. Confirm on the wire, where a replay shows byte-identical timeStamp, path and inode on every delivery — as it does here, for an event dated 2026-08-14.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 20,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "cee-prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(cee_events_received_total[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(cee_cepa_heartbeats_total[5m])), 0.0001)",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Publisher silence (seconds since last request)",
      "description": "Per CEE server. A CEE server, not a NAS Data Mover: a Data Mover that stops publishing into a healthy CEE server is not visible here.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "time() - cee_cepa_last_request_unix_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "{{remote}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 30
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 60
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "cee-prometheus"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Handshakes per publisher",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(cee_cepa_registrations_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "{{remote}} register",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "rate(cee_cepa_heartbeats_total[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "{{remote}} heartbeat",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "cee-prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "axisSoftMin": 0
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byRegexp",
              "options": ".*heartbeat$"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    6
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "cee-prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Registrations and heartbeats are separate series because they mean different things. Only a CEE server sends RegisterRequest; arrays publishing directly (PowerStore Data Movers, OneFS nodes) only ever heartbeat, so zero registrations against a healthy heartbeat rate is normal for them. Until v5.4.2 both were counted as registrations, so this panel showed a registration rate for publishers that had never registered.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
